{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-68p9-83h6-5wpj","published":"2026-11-12T22:08:21Z","modified":"2026-11-12T22:15:03.756635963Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-126069"],"summary":"Action View: Possible XSS vulnerability in tag helpers","details":"### Impact\nThe fix for [CVE-2026-33168](https://github.com/rails/rails/security/advisories/GHSA-v55j-83pf-r9cq) skips blank HTML attribute names in Action View tag helpers, but it tests the name before converting it to a string. A Symbol name made only of whitespace, such as `:\" \"`, is not blank, because `Symbol#blank?` is `Symbol#empty?`, so it reaches the attribute escaping, which emits an attribute with no name and produces malformed HTML. The asset tag helpers, such as `image_tag`, `video_tag` and `audio_tag`, symbolize their options, so a whitespace String name passed to them takes the same path. A carefully crafted attribute value could then be misinterpreted by the browser as a separate attribute name, possibly leading to XSS. Applications that allow users to specify custom HTML attribute names are affected.\n\n### Releases\nThe fixed releases are available at the normal locations.\n\nPatches for those who cannot upgrade at once:\n- 8.1: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/9190210606ffe52f92fdc75637f8ff69404f22c8.patch\n- 8.0: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/f47452533e1f28d847c63181b9d5f8b7243ef9a4.patch\n\n### Credit\nThis issue was responsibly reported by HackerOne researcher [thepo1es](https://hackerone.com/thepo1es).","affected":[{"package":{"name":"actionview","ecosystem":"RubyGems","purl":"pkg:gem/actionview"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"8.1.0.beta1"},{"fixed":"8.1.4.1"}]}],"versions":["8.1.0","8.1.0.beta1","8.1.0.rc1","8.1.1","8.1.2","8.1.2.1","8.1.3","8.1.3.1","8.1.4"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/11/GHSA-68p9-83h6-5wpj/GHSA-68p9-83h6-5wpj.json"}},{"package":{"name":"actionview","ecosystem":"